REASONING

The structured row files Northwind under "Transportation & Logistics" with a description about helping forwarders "modernize back-office operations", and the posting's title reads like an operator seat. But the procedure says structured fields lie and that self-description counts wherever the company writes it. The homepage capture is unambiguous: "the AI operations platform for freight", a platform with pricing tiers, integrations and a customer logo wall, deployed at 40+ forwarders. The posting's own About paragraph repeats it: "We build the AI operations platform freight companies run their back office on." The company sells the capability; its customers are the operators. Per the ICP's illustrative rule — a company whose product IS the capability we sell is out — this is the vendor_of_the_capability class. The industry tag describes who it sells to, not what it is.

{"decision": "drop", "drop_class": "vendor_of_the_capability", "rationale": "Homepage and the posting's own About paragraph describe an AI operations platform sold to forwarders and 3PLs (pricing, integrations, customer logos); the logistics industry tag names its customers' vertical, not its own business."}
